I have United States, I have Denmark, I have Ireland, I have the UK, I have France again, Canada. So it's not one place. It is almost a global shooting. And I don't know. Somebody said, imagine an entire nation living like this. Why did strangers who knew nothing about Wafa take it upon themselves to hurt him? Do technology in modern life and the anonymity they offer make us less caring as human beings? On today's show, building empathy in a connected and confrontational world.
我有美国、丹麦、爱尔兰、英国、法国还有加拿大。所以这不是一个地方。这几乎是一场全球性的枪击。而且我不知道。有人说，想象一下整个国家都过着这样的生活。为什么对瓦法一无所知的陌生人会自作主张去伤害他？科技和现代生活以及它们提供的匿名性是否让我们作为人类变得不那么有同情心了？在今天的节目中，我们将在一个互联且对抗的世界中建立同理心。

