00:06:30.000 --> 00:07:14.000
And it was just very confusing. And it felt, I think, to all three of us, like I would really have to be. have to choose one of my parents and give up on really knowing the other. But I knew that I had to try for all of our sake. So I did, and I kind of kept working at it and eventually got better, learned to tune myself to my parents' different frequencies. And that kind of saved me as a kid. I think empathy saved me. Not because it's easy, it was work. I always think of my parents' divorce as an empathy gym for me that forced me to work out my ability. to care about and understand other people.
这真的很让人困惑。而且我想，对我们三个人来说，这感觉就像我真的必须去。必须在父母之间做出选择，并放弃真正了解另一方的机会。但我知道为了我们所有人的利益，我必须尝试。所以我做了，我一直在努力，最终做得越来越好，学会了调整自己以适应父母不同的频率。那种经历在某种程度上拯救了我，作为一个孩子。我认为同理心拯救了我。不是因为它容易，这需要付出努力。我总是把父母的离婚看作是我的同理心健身房，它强迫我锻炼自己去关心和理解其他人的能力。

